{"title":"Career roadmap — Policy Analyst","role":"Policy Analyst","summary":"A Policy Analyst researches public problems, evaluates policies, analyses evidence and develops recommendations for governments, think tanks, consulting firms, NGOs, international organisations and public-sector institutions. The strongest profile combines political economy + public policy + economics + research methodology + data analysis + clear policy communication.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Political Economy / Public Policy / Governance"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build economics, political science, governance, research and quantitative-analysis foundations"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work as Policy Researcher/Analyst in think tanks, consulting, government programmes, NGOs or research institutions"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Specialise in a policy domain and progress toward Senior Policy Analyst/Policy Advisor roles"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead policy research, programme evaluation, advisory teams or public-policy institutions"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Political economy and governance foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political science"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Indian Constitution"},{"text":"Indian political system"},{"text":"Public institutions"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Development economics"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Political economy"},{"text":"Public finance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Critical thinking"},{"text":"Argument construction"},{"text":"Policy reading"},{"text":"Current-affairs analysis"},{"text":"Research skills"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Start reading:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government reports"},{"text":"Budgets"},{"text":"Parliamentary documents"},{"text":"Economic surveys"},{"text":"Policy papers"},{"text":"Regulatory documents"},{"text":"Development reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Policy research and analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy cycle"},{"text":"Problem definition"},{"text":"Stakeholder analysis"},{"text":"Policy design"},{"text":"Cost-benefit analysis"},{"text":"Cost-effectiveness analysis"},{"text":"Programme evaluation"},{"text":"Impact assessment"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Public finance"},{"text":"Regulatory policy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Technology:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SQL basics"},{"text":"R or Python"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"GIS basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Policy specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a policy domain:"},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Example areas"],"rows":[[{"text":"Economic Policy"},{"text":"Growth, inflation, taxation"}],[{"text":"Public Finance"},{"text":"Government spending, budgets"}],[{"text":"Education Policy"},{"text":"Schools, higher education"}],[{"text":"Health Policy"},{"text":"Healthcare systems"}],[{"text":"Climate Policy"},{"text":"Climate and energy"}],[{"text":"Technology Policy"},{"text":"AI, digital regulation"}],[{"text":"Urban Policy"},{"text":"Housing, transport, cities"}],[{"text":"Agricultural Policy"},{"text":"Rural development, farming"}],[{"text":"Social Policy"},{"text":"Poverty, welfare"}],[{"text":"Foreign Policy"},{"text":"Diplomacy, international affairs"}],[{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Public administration"}],[{"text":"Labour Policy"},{"text":"Employment and skills"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Build a portfolio containin