nior Research Fellow","Research Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Government pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy/Research Intern","Policy Associate","Policy Analyst","Senior Policy Analyst","Policy Advisor","Senior Policy Advisor"]},{"type":"h","text":"Consulting pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Analyst","Policy Consultant","Senior Consultant","Manager","Principal/Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Development pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Programme Intern","Programme Analyst","Policy Specialist","Senior Specialist","Programme Manager","Policy/Programme Director"]},{"type":"note","label":"Emerging specialisations","text":"2030–2040"},{"type":"h","text":"1. AI Policy"},{"type":"p","text":"Growing areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI regulation"},{"text":"Algorithmic accountability"},{"text":"AI safety"},{"text":"Data governance"},{"text":"Digital rights"},{"text":"AI and employment"},{"text":"Public-sector AI"},{"text":"Responsible AI"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Climate Policy"},{"type":"p","text":"Policy professionals will increasingly work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Carbon markets"},{"text":"Climate finance"},{"text":"Energy transition"},{"text":"Renewable energy"},{"text":"Adaptation"},{"text":"Climate migration"},{"text":"Green industrial policy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Digital Public Policy"},{"type":"p","text":"Major areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital identity"},{"text":"Digital public infrastructure"},{"text":"Data governance"},{"text":"Cybersecurity policy"},{"text":"Digital competition"},{"text":"Platform regulation"},{"text":"Digital inclusion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Evidence-Based Governance"},{"type":"p","text":"Governments and organisations increasingly need professionals who can connect:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy","Data","Programme","Outcome","Evaluation"]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Urban Policy Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Combining:"},{"type":"flow","items":["GIS","Economics","Public Policy","Data"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"can support decisions around:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Housing"},{"text":"Transport"},{"text":"Pollution"},{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"Public services"},{"text":"Urban expansion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Geopolitical and Economic Risk"},{"type":"p","text":"Policy analysts can specialise in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trade policy"},{"text":"Sanctions"},{"text":"Supply chains"},{"text":"Energy security"},{"text":"Geopolitics"},{"text":"International investment"},{"text":"Economic security"}]},{"type":"note","label":"2040–2046","text":"How the role evolves"},{"type":"p","text":"The future Policy Analyst will increasingly operate as:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy Researcher","Economist","Data Analyst","Technology Specialist","Strategic Advisor"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"AI will help with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Document analysis"},{"text":"Policy comparison"},{"text":"Literature reviews"},{"text":"Data processing"},{"text":"Scenario modelling"},{"text":"Regulatory monitoring"},{"text":"Evidence synthesis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But human professionals remain responsible for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Defining the policy problem"},{"text":"Understanding political/institutional context"},{"text":"Assessing trade-offs"},{"text":"Stakeholder engagement"},{"text":"Ethical judgement"},{"text":"Making recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Policy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy analysis"},{"text":"Policy design"},{"text":"Programme evaluation"},{"text":"Regulatory analysis"},{"text":"Stakeholder analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Economics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microeconomics"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Development economics"},{"text":"Public economics"},{"text":"Cost-benefit analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Evidence synthesis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"R/Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Econometrics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Governance"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indian Constitution"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Government institutions"},{"text":"Public finance"},{"text":"Regulatory systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy briefs"},{"text":"Research reports"},{"text":"Presentations"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Executive summaries"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["2026–27: Economics + political science + governance fundamentals","2027–28: Research methods + statistics + policy analysis","2028–29: Data analysis + policy portfolio + internship","2029–30: Policy Research Assistant / Policy Intern","2030–33: Policy Analyst / Research Associate","2033–36: Senior Policy Analyst / Policy Consultant","2036–40: Policy Advisor / Research Fellow / Policy Manager","2040–46: Policy Director / Research Director / Senior Policy Advisor"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Economy/Public Policy","MPP/MA Public Policy or Economics","Policy Research","Econometrics","Data Analysis","Programme Evaluation","Strong Policy Writing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Key principle","text":"A strong Policy Analyst does not merely describe a social problem. They should be able to define the problem, analyse evidence, understand economic and political trade-offs, evaluate policy alternatives, quantify likely impacts and communicate a practical recommendation clearly to decision-makers."},{"type":"p","text":"1597 | BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours) | Political Economy / Public Policy / Governance | Civil Services Aspirant"}]}]}